      "message": "test: Remove `BOOST_FAIL` and add info in descriptor_tests\n\nThe `BOOST_FAIL` here is used to exit the test based on a condition, but\nwe can use `REQUIRE` directly. The context string is only printed on\nfailure to my knowledge and this is not called on a child thread so\nthere is no behavior change.\n\nThe `descriptor_tests` uses `BOOST_TEST_INFO` to add the descriptor if\nthe next condition fails, but there are some other places that also\nprint the public or private descriptor. Seems useful throughout this\nwhole funciton body to attach the private and public descriptor as\ncontext.\n\nFound in 35713 as low usage macros\n\nref:\n- https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/latest/libs/test/doc/html/boost_test/utf_reference/testout_reference/test_output_macro_info.html\n- https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/latest/libs/test/doc/html/boost_test/utf_reference/testout_reference/test_output_macro_context_sticky.html\n- https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/latest/libs/test/doc/html/boost_test/utf_reference/testing_tool_ref/assertion_boost_fail.html",
